  "notes": [
    "dataset is SYNTHETIC and controlled (PIL, seed 1234, no photographs): OCR strings, coloured-shape counts on a 3x3 grid, fixed compositions for ROUGE-L, and 3-4 frame motion sequences. Every image is byte-reproducible from make_p6_vlm.py; per-file sha256, prompt and reference answer are in data/p6_vlm/manifest.json. It is a controlled capability probe, not a natural-image benchmark.",
    "dense baseline generation is the same model with permuted-but-unskipped weights (tau=0 path); the tau=0 check verifies this is bit-comparable to the unpermuted model (max|dlogit|=0.00e+00, identical token ids on all 52 samples).",
    "scoring: OCR = exact match on the first non-empty answer line after stripping quotes/backticks and non-alphanumerics (the model often appends commentary); counting = first integer in the answer equals the rendered count; scene = ROUGE-L F1 against a reference sentence; motion = exact match of the first answer word (direction / bigger / smaller). Aggregate acc is the unweighted mean per-sample score across all families, so scene/motion contribute fractional ROUGE-style credit; acc_by_family gives the per-family view.",
    "tau rows use the per-layer theta quantiles of per-token block energies calibrated on 8 images from this set (ocr, ocr, ocr, counting, counting, scene, scene, motion); actual_skip is measured on the eval pass, energy_captured is the retained activation energy fraction.",
    "feature rel-L2 is on the connector image features, logit rel-L2 on the prefill logits at the last prompt position, averaged over samples. first_div is the mean index of the first token where the greedy answer differs from dense (gen_len is the cap).",
    "TIMING: CPU fp32, 16 threads (OMP_WAIT_POLICY=passive), the real AVX-512 kernel down_skip_avx512_auto2 replaces BOTH down projections (vision fc2 and text down_proj); a warm-up forward+prefill runs before every timed config, then medians are taken. The dense row uses plain F.linear (torch/MKL). Kernel and F.linear are both given the same thread count, so the comparison is honest but kernel-vs-MKL: at low tau the mask bookkeeping (energy + threshold + numpy/ctypes hand-off) can cost more than the skipped FMAs, see kernel_micro for the pure GEMM comparison at the same shapes.",
    "GPU timing is deliberately not attempted beyond a liveness probe: the 8 GB GPU is shared with another job (usable). The P5 numbers in results/p5_smolvlm.json remain the GPU reference for the masking path.",
    "p5_smolvlm.json is untouched; this file is the 58-sample replacement for its 4-prompt VQA weakness."
  ]
}